    {
      "id": 2,
      "slug": "eps-spine-replacement",
      "title": "EPS Spine Replacement",
      "description_html": "",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "type": "image",
          "variant": "full",
          "style": {
            "background_type": "LIGHT",
            "card_mode": "WHITE",
            "image_opacity": 0.5,
            "image_opacity_color": "#000000",
            "zoom_on_click": false,
            "attached_to_next": false,
            "padding_top": 0,
            "padding_bottom": 0,
            "custom_padding_top": 0,
            "custom_padding_bottom": 0,
            "marker_color_contrast": "AUTO",
            "entrance_animation": true
          },
          "image_role": "decorative",
          "media": {
            "path": "resources/images/why-4.png",
            "alt": "Why_4.png",
            "source_asset": "Why_4.png",
            "mime_type": "image/png",
            "bytes": 9256,
            "dimensions": {
              "originalWidth": 1680,
              "originalHeight": 222
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "type": "text",
          "variant": "paragraph",
          "style": {
            "background_type": "COLOR",
            "background_color": "#f1f1f1",
            "attached_to_next": false,
            "padding_top": 3,
            "padding_bottom": 3,
            "marker_color_contrast": "AUTO"
          },
          "body_html": "<p>In traditional data center architectures, the spine layer consists of high-density <strong>Electrical Packet Switches (EPS)</strong>. By replacing these electrical spine switches with <strong>Optical Circuit Switching</strong>, operators can create a flat, optically switched layer connecting all leaf switches directly.</p><p><strong>Google</strong> demonstrated this with their <strong>Jupiter Evolving</strong> deployment. Replacing the EPS spine with OCS yielded a <strong>41 percent reduction</strong> in network power consumption and a <strong>30 percent reduction</strong> in capital expenditure. Furthermore, it enabled a <strong>five-fold increase</strong> in network throughput and facilitated faster, incremental deployments.</p><p>Explore the graphic below to understand the key differences between these architectures.</p>"
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "type": "labeled_graphic",
          "variant": "labeledgraphic",
          "style": {
            "background_type": "COLOR",
            "background_color": "#f1f1f1",
            "zoom_on_click": true,
            "attached_to_next": false,
            "padding_top": 3,
            "padding_bottom": 3,
            "media_width": "1",
            "marker_color_contrast": "AUTO",
            "media_width_variant": "medium"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "title": "The EPS Before State",
              "x": "24.208831787109375",
              "y": "33.53615735573744",
              "icon": "01",
              "description_html": "<p>In a standard 3-tier Clos network, leaf switches connect to power-hungry EPS spine blocks.</p><p></p>"
            },
            {
              "title": "The OCS After State",
              "x": "75.02357119605655",
              "y": "47.61243386243386",
              "icon": "01",
              "description_html": "<p>The EPS spine is replaced by an optical Data Center Network Interconnect layer.</p>"
            },
            {
              "title": "Rate Independence",
              "x": "73.57142857142858",
              "y": "70.7936507936508",
              "icon": "01",
              "description_html": "<p>Because the OCS spine is rate-agnostic, operators can upgrade leaf and interconnect speeds without facing constraints from the spine layer.</p>"
            }
          ],
          "media": {
            "path": "resources/images/core.jpg",
            "alt": "Core.jpg",
            "source_asset": "Core.jpg",
            "mime_type": "image/jpeg",
            "bytes": 97586,
            "dimensions": {
              "originalWidth": 1680,
              "originalHeight": 945
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "type": "text",
          "variant": "subheading",
          "style": {
            "background_type": "COLOR",
            "background_color": "#f2f2f1",
            "attached_to_next": false,
            "padding_top": 3,
            "padding_bottom": 0,
            "marker_color_contrast": "AUTO"
          },
          "heading_html": "<p>While spine replacement optimizes traffic across the entire data center, optical switching can also be deployed <span style=\"color: #8cc53f; text-decoration: inherit\" data-color-scope=\"inner\">directly between compute nodes</span> to accelerate specific AI workloads.</p>"
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "type": "image",
          "variant": "full",
          "style": {
            "background_type": "LIGHT",
            "card_mode": "WHITE",
            "image_opacity": 0.5,
